    "notes": {
        "f3fe8b48-b36f-4f63-9ce7-9510a2f7b8d5": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 320,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 256,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\n- The workspace must have **at least two users** (ListUsers `$[0]` / `$[1]`); requester and approver must differ.\n- Only the `created` port is asserted. Approve/Reject needs a human click in Slack, so the task stays **pending** after the run.\n- At *decisionBy* (+60 min) the plugin's due job fires the `due` webhook at this flow. If the flow is only **stopped**, the webhook fails with 400 and the task stays in `error`, retried with a growing backoff until the flow runs again or the 60-day cleanup removes it. Only if the flow is **deleted** (404/410) is the task removed right away (slack 5.5.2, issue #2901). Check the plugin logs for `slack-trigger-webhook-error` / `slack-trigger-webhook-gone`."
        }
    }
